module oked-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6 }

// The Eastern District of Oklahoma's own civil periods, computed under the
// federal rules: the local rules supplement the Federal Rules of Civil
// Procedure (LCvR 1.1, 1.2(a)), so FRCP 6(a) counts them. A motion for
// leave to file an oversized brief is filed no later than one day before
// the brief is due (E.D. Okla. LCvR 7.1(c)). A non-dispositive motion or
// objection not opposed within 14 days may be deemed confessed (LCvR
// 7.1(d)); if a dispositive motion is not opposed, the Court may allow an
// additional 14 days to show cause, and a motion for confession of
// judgment may be granted 14 days after filing (LCvR 7.1(g)); those set
// what the Court may do, not a party's filing, and stay notes. The Court
// Clerk may grant a defendant a first extension, not over 14 days, to
// answer (LCvR 7.1(h)); that bounds an order and stays a note. A matter
// under advisement more than 90 days may be noticed (LCvR 7.1(l)). Paper
// copies of oversized documents are delivered within 3 business days
// (LCvR 7.1(n)) and exhibits are shown to opposing counsel 3 business days
// before the pretrial order (LCvR 39.4), periods FRCP 6(a) does not count;
// and the attorneys meet the courtroom deputy within 7 days of the trial
// date (LCvR 43.1(b)), a window the rule does not anchor to one side. In
// a removed case the jury demand runs on FRCP 38 and 81 (LCvR 81.1), which
// lit/frcp encodes. The earlier E.D. Okla. outline's FRCP flow and its
// decisions (Twombly, Iqbal, Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby,
// Matsushita, Unitherm, Bowles v. Russell, Hamer, Microsoft Corp. v.
// Baker and the Tenth Circuit's Robbins v. Oklahoma) are FRCP and FRAP
// authority and belong to lit/frcp and lit/frap; they are removed here:
// no reporter text is vendored.
/// A brief: at most 25 typewritten pages without leave of Court (E.D.
/// Okla. LCvR 7.1(c)).
limit motion-brief { pages <= 25 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 7.1(c)" } cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 7.1(c)"
/// A reply or supplemental brief: at most 10 pages unless the Court
/// authorizes more (E.D. Okla. LCvR 7.1(e)).
limit reply-brief { pages <= 10 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 7.1(e)" } cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 7.1(e)"

/// A civil action, suit or proceeding is filed (E.D. Okla. LCvR 3.2).
event ActionFiled()
/// The motion to proceed in forma pauperis is denied (E.D. Okla. LCvR
/// 3.3(d)).
event PauperMotionDenied()
/// A motion or objection is filed (E.D. Okla. LCvR 7.1(d)).
event MotionFiled() paper motion-brief
/// The response to a motion or objection is filed (E.D. Okla. LCvR
/// 7.1(e)).
event ResponseFiled() paper motion-brief
/// The reply brief is filed (E.D. Okla. LCvR 7.1(e)).
event ReplyFiled() paper reply-brief
/// The date the Joint Status Report is to be submitted (E.D. Okla. LCvR
/// 16.1(a)).
event JointStatusReportDue()
/// A settlement conference is set (E.D. Okla. LCvR 16.2).
event SettlementConferenceSet()
/// A party to the civil case files bankruptcy, or an involuntary
/// proceeding is commenced against it (E.D. Okla. LCvR 21.1).
event PartyBankruptcyFiled()
/// A deposition is scheduled to be taken (E.D. Okla. LCvR 30.1(a)).
event DepositionScheduled()
/// Trial is set (E.D. Okla. LCvR 30.1(f)).
event TrialSet()
/// Judgment is entered (E.D. Okla. LCvR 54.1(a), 54.2(a)).
event JudgmentEntered()
/// The bill of costs is filed (E.D. Okla. LCvR 54.1(b)).
event BillOfCostsFiled()
/// The motion for attorney fees is filed (E.D. Okla. LCvR 54.2(c)).
event FeeMotionFiled()
/// The motion for admission pro hac vice is granted (E.D. Okla. LCvR
/// 83.3(c)).
event ProHacViceGranted()
/// In a bankruptcy case, the first meeting of creditors is held (E.D.
/// Okla. LCvR 84.1).
event CreditorsMeetingHeld()
/// A motion to withdraw the reference is served (E.D. Okla. LCvR 84.1).
event WithdrawalMotionServed()

/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 3.2: except under LCvR 3.3, 3.4, 3.5 or a case order,
/// the filing fee is paid within 7 days of the filing of a civil action,
/// suit or proceeding, or it is subject to immediate dismissal without
/// prejudice to refiling.
deadline filing-fee-period: 7.days after ActionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 3.2"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 3.3(d): if the motion to proceed in forma pauperis is
/// denied, the filing party has 21 days, unless the Court specifies a
/// different time, to pay the filing fees.
deadline pauper-fee-period: 21.days after PauperMotionDenied() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 3.3(d)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 7.1(d): each party opposing a motion or objection files
/// and serves a response within 14 days from the date the motion or
/// objection was filed.
deadline motion-response-period: 14.days after MotionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 7.1(d)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 7.1(e): a reply brief on new matters in the response
/// may be filed within 14 days after the response is filed; the Court may
/// increase or reduce the time.
deadline reply-period: 14.days after ResponseFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 7.1(e)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 16.1(a): to prepare the Joint Status Report, counsel
/// and pro se parties confer at least 14 days before the date it is to be
/// submitted.
deadline status-report-conference-period: 14.days before JointStatusReportDue() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 16.1(a)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 16.2(e): a governmental entity unable to send a
/// representative with full settlement authority files and delivers its
/// motion to proceed with limited authority no later than 14 days before
/// the conference.
deadline limited-authority-motion-period: 14.days before SettlementConferenceSet() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 16.2(e)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 16.2(f): unless the Court orders otherwise, the
/// settlement statement, at most 5 pages, is submitted to the settlement
/// judge and served at least 7 days before the settlement conference.
deadline settlement-statement-period: 7.days before SettlementConferenceSet() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 16.2(f)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 21.1: when a party to a civil case files bankruptcy, or
/// an involuntary proceeding is commenced against it, notice is given
/// within 7 days of the bankruptcy filing by a formal notice in the civil
/// case.
deadline bankruptcy-notice-period: 7.days after PartyBankruptcyFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 21.1"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 30.1(a)(1): subject to an order enlarging or shortening
/// the time, a subpoena to compel a witness to attend a deposition is
/// served on the witness at least 7 days before the deposition.
deadline deposition-subpoena-period: 7.days before DepositionScheduled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 30.1(a)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 30.1(a)(2): reasonable notice to parties under FRCP
/// 30(b)(1) of the taking of a deposition is 7 days.
deadline deposition-notice-period: 7.days before DepositionScheduled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 30.1(a)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 30.1(f): except by order of the Court, trial
/// depositions may be taken on reasonable notice up to 14 days before
/// trial.
deadline trial-deposition-period: 14.days before TrialSet() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 30.1(f)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 54.1(a): a prevailing party seeking costs under 28
/// U.S.C. § 1920 files and serves the bill of costs and its brief not more
/// than 14 days after entry of judgment.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 14.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 54.1(a)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 54.1(b): objections to the allowance of costs are filed
/// within 14 days from the date the bill of costs was filed.
deadline costs-objection-period: 14.days after BillOfCostsFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 54.1(b)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 54.2(a): the motion for attorney fees, with its brief
/// and affidavit, is filed and served not more than 14 days after entry of
/// judgment (as FRCP 54(d)(2)(B) provides).
deadline fee-motion-period: 14.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 54.2(a)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 54.2(c): responses in opposition to the allowance of
/// attorney fees are filed within 14 days from the date the motion is
/// filed.
deadline fee-response-period: 14.days after FeeMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 54.2(c)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 83.4(c): an attorney appearing pro hac vice files an
/// Entry of Appearance and registers for electronic case filing within 7
/// days after the motion is granted.
deadline pro-hac-vice-appearance-period: 7.days after ProHacViceGranted() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 83.4(c)"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 84.1: a motion to withdraw the reference of a
/// bankruptcy case is filed and served within 14 days after the first
/// meeting of creditors is held (in an adversary proceeding or contested
/// matter, with the movant's first responsive pleading, not encoded).
deadline withdrawal-motion-period: 14.days after CreditorsMeetingHeld() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 84.1"
/// E.D. Okla. LCvR 84.1: responses to a motion to withdraw the reference
/// are filed with the bankruptcy clerk within 14 days from service of the
/// motion; replies only with leave of the bankruptcy court.
deadline withdrawal-response-period: 14.days after WithdrawalMotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "E.D. Okla. LCvR 84.1"
